# Today I Learned — 2026-04-04
Structured deep cloning in modern JS: structuredClone preserves Dates, Maps, Sets, RegExps, ArrayBuffers, BigInts, circular refs, etc. Use it when available; otherwise fall back to a lossy JSON approach.

```js
/**
 * deepClone(obj): deep clones a value.
 * - Uses global structuredClone when available (preserves rich types + cycles).
 * - Falls back to JSON-based clone (loses functions, Dates, Maps, Sets, etc.).
 *
 * Usage:
 *   const copy = deepClone(original);
 */
export function deepClone(obj) {
  if (typeof structuredClone === "function") {
    return structuredClone(obj);
  }
  return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(obj)); // lossy fallback
}

